describe_operation {"operationId":"postV1ContentPreviewEmail"} → {"operationId":"postV1ContentPreviewEmail","method":"POST","path":"/v1/content/preview-email","summary":"Write one cold email for a brand and a sample recipient","description":"Proxy to content-generation-service POST /preview-email. Writes the first email of the sequence the product would send, for a brand of the calling org and a sample recipient, before any campaign exists. The LLM spend is billed to the calling org; an org that cannot afford it gets 402 with the downstream body forwarded field-for-field. Body + response shapes are owned by the downstream service.

Request body: documented from content-generation-service POST /preview-email, which owns and validates it; the gateway forwards it unchanged.

Response: documented from content-generation-service POST /preview-email, which owns it; the gateway forwards it unchanged. Its full document: GET /v1/platform/services/content-generation.","params":[],"body":{"type":"object","properties":{"brandId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"A brand of the calling org. Its site must already be readable by brand-service."},"recipient":{"type":"object","properties":{"firstName":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"lastName":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"title":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The recipient's job title."},"companyName":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"companyDomain":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The recipient's company website or domain."},"headline":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The recipient's own one-line professional headline."},"companyIndustry":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"companyDescription":{"type":"string","minLength":1}},"required":["firstName","lastName","title","companyName"]},"audience":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The audience / segment the sample recipient was found in, in plain English. Given to the model as context."},"offerId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"Which offer of the brand to pitch. Required by brand-service only when the brand sells several offers."},"qualification":{"type":"object","properties":{"domain":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"The company the checks ran on."},"checks":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"question":{"type":"string","description":"The check's question, as the offer states it."},"mode":{"type":"string","description":"must_pass (Hard filter) or mention (Bonus)."},"verdict":{"type":"string","description":"yes | no | unavailable | not_checked"},"evidence":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"reason":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"screenshotUrl":{"type":"string","nullable":true}},"required":["question"],"additionalProperties":{"nullable":true}}}},"required":["checks"],"additionalProperties":{"nullable":true},"description":"The offer's checks run on the recipient's company, exactly as lead-service serves them for that company (the same shape as a lead's `qualification`): { domain, checks: [{ question, mode ('must_pass' | 'mention'), verdict ('yes' | 'no' | 'unavailable' | 'not_checked'), evidence, reason, screenshotUrl, ... }] }. Forward it verbatim. Rendered to the model in the same "Checks we ran on their company" block as a campaign email (context only). Part of the stored preview's identity: changed results write a new email, the same results are answered from storage. Absent or `checks: []` = the preview is written exactly as without it."},"strategyId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":100,"description":"Write the example the way a campaign running this play of the cold-email pipe would: a features-service strategy id on `sales-cold-email-outreach|lead_found_to_conversation` (`offer-emails-only` = leads with something given for free, `named-emails-only` = names the brand and pitches it, `blind-emails-only` = never names the brand, asks about the problem first; any other play of the pipe works too). The email is written with the template + model of the workflow that play's campaign would run (its measured best, else the first workflow it allows in the leg ranking). Absent = the best mature cold-email workflow, as before. A strategy with no play on the pipe = 400 `code: UNKNOWN_STRATEGY`."}},"required":["brandId","recipient"]},"answers":[{"status":"200","description":"The written email","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"Stored preview id."},"brandId":{"type":"string"},"brandName":{"type":"string"},"recipient":{"type":"object","properties":{"firstName":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"lastName":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"title":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The recipient's job title."},"companyName":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"companyDomain":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The recipient's company website or domain."},"headline":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The recipient's own one-line professional headline."},"companyIndustry":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"companyDescription":{"type":"string","minLength":1}},"required":["firstName","lastName","title","companyName"]},"subject":{"type":"string"},"bodyText":{"type":"string","description":"The first email of the sequence the product would send, as plain text."},"bodyHtml":{"type":"string"},"model":{"type":"string","description":"Resolved model id that wrote the email."},"promptType":{"type":"string","description":"The prompt template that wrote the email: the best mature cold-email workflow's, when it was written."},"modelAlias":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"The model alias the workflow states (e.g. glm-pro). null on a preview stored before the preview followed the best mature workflow."},"workflowSlug":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"The workflow whose template + model wrote the email (the best mature cold-email workflow at the time). null on a preview stored before the preview followed it."},"highlights":{"type":"array","nullable":true,"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string","description":"A sentence or clause of bodyText, verbatim."},"start":{"type":"integer","description":"Offset of text in bodyText (JS string index): bodyText.slice(start, end) === text."},"end":{"type":"integer"},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["prospect","brand","audience","instruction"],"description":"Where the reason comes from. prospect: a fact about the recipient or their company (the data sent in `recipient`). brand: a fact about the sender's company, read from its website by brand-service. audience: the segment sent in `audience`. instruction: a writing rule of the email template (greeting, diagnostic question, call to action), not a fact."},"source":{"type":"string","description":"The exact input: `recipient.<field>`, `check.<n>` (the n-th check of `qualification`), `audience`, `brand.name`, `brand.<extracted field key>` (e.g. brand.customerPainPoints), or `instruction`."},"sourceLabel":{"type":"string","description":"Plain-English name of that input."},"sourceValue":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"The input's actual value as the model received it. null for instruction."},"reason":{"type":"string","description":"Why this text is there, in one sentence, as reported by the model that wrote the email."}},"required":["text","start","end","kind","source","sourceLabel","sourceValue","reason"]},"description":"Why each sentence of bodyText exists and which input it rests on, in body order, non-overlapping. Reported by a SECOND completion that reads the finished email (the writing call is the plain /generate call), then checked here: every text is verbatim in bodyText and every source is an input actually sent; anything failing a check is dropped, so a sentence may carry no highlight. null when that second call failed (the email is served anyway) or for a preview stored before highlights existed."},"cached":{"type":"boolean","description":"true when this brand + recipient was already written and the stored email is returned (nothing billed)."},"createdAt":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","brandId","brandName","recipient","subject","bodyText","bodyHtml","model","promptType","modelAlias","workflowSlug","highlights","cached","createdAt"]}}],"needsTheirYes":false}

describe_operation {"operationId":"patchV1SalesFunnelCampaignsById"} → {"operationId":"patchV1SalesFunnelCampaignsById","method":"PATCH","path":"/v1/sales-funnel-campaigns/{id}","summary":"Run or pause the whole sales funnel campaign","description":"Proxy to campaign-service PATCH /sales-funnel-campaigns/{id}. A SALES FUNNEL CAMPAIGN (owner 2026-10-10) is brand x offer x sales funnel: it owns one unit (an ordinary campaign) per pipe of the funnel and is run or paused as a whole. Its money is the funnel's caps at billing (GET /v1/brands/{brandId}/offers/{offerId}/sales-funnels/{salesFunnelId}/caps); no max budget = held unfunded. The org is the authenticated one. Status and body (with `reason` on a refusal) relayed verbatim. HOW each pipe behaves is fixed by the funnel's plays (`<leg>@<channel>~<strategy id>` in the funnel id; see the Plays tag: tactic, strategy, play on a pipe, a funnel carrying it, a campaign on that funnel). To change a behaviour (for example replies that carry an offer document as an attachment), launch a campaign on a funnel carrying the right play, created with `status: stopped` until the client agrees. Body { status: activate | stop } forwarded untouched; every unit moves with it.

Request body: documented from campaign-service PATCH /sales-funnel-campaigns/{id}, which owns and validates it; the gateway forwards it unchanged.

